target: internal/learn/learn.go
verify: go test ./internal/learn/ -count=1 -run 'TestALeadingDateIsNotWrittenTwice'
expect: the entry's date is wrong or written twice
why:    add stamps its own date, so text passed as "2026-10-20: …" lands as "- <today>: 2026-10-20: …", two dates on one entry, and the second one is never bumped.
--- old
		text = leadingDate.ReplaceAllString(text, "")
--- new
		_ = leadingDate
